WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.201 --> 00:00:02.568
-Welcome back
to "The Tonight Show."

00:00:02.568 --> 00:00:04.337
Well, everybody, making jokes
during times like these

00:00:04.337 --> 00:00:07.473
is difficult, but it's my job
to try and make people laugh

00:00:07.473 --> 00:00:10.042
and feel better, even if just
for a little while.

00:00:10.042 --> 00:00:12.812
So, with that in mind,
let's tell some jokes.

00:00:12.812 --> 00:00:14.981
Last night, President Trump
made another stop

00:00:14.981 --> 00:00:17.683
on his great American
COVID tour,

00:00:17.683 --> 00:00:19.486
this time in Pennsylvania,

00:00:19.486 --> 00:00:21.487
at the Pittsburgh
International Airport.

00:00:21.487 --> 00:00:23.889
There was quite a turnout
at the airport rally.

00:00:23.889 --> 00:00:27.193
Take a look at this photo.

00:00:27.193 --> 00:00:29.061
For any parents watching,
if you ran out of

00:00:29.061 --> 00:00:31.464
"Where's Waldo?" books for your
kids during quarantine,

00:00:31.464 --> 00:00:33.098
just hand them this photo
and tell them to find

00:00:33.098 --> 00:00:35.301
a Trump supporter
wearing a mask.

00:00:35.301 --> 00:00:37.536
[ Laughter ]

00:00:37.536 --> 00:00:39.071
You gotta give Trump credit
for one thing --

00:00:39.071 --> 00:00:41.307
this had to be the first time
in history people were excited

00:00:41.307 --> 00:00:43.843
to spend a Tuesday night
at the Pittsburgh airport.

00:00:43.843 --> 00:00:44.877
[ Laughter ]

00:00:44.877 --> 00:00:46.713
Trump was on stage
for 90 minutes,

00:00:46.713 --> 00:00:48.915
and I think there was some
things he could've skipped,

00:00:48.915 --> 00:00:52.484
like here when he questioned why
Joe Biden always wears a mask.

00:00:52.484 --> 00:00:53.653
Listen to this.

00:00:53.653 --> 00:00:55.588
-He feels good about the mask,
and that's okay.

00:00:55.588 --> 00:00:57.723
You know what?
Whatever makes you feel good.

00:00:57.723 --> 00:01:00.560
He feels good.
He feels good.

00:01:00.560 --> 00:01:03.996
I mean, honestly, what the hell
did he spend all that money

00:01:03.996 --> 00:01:06.265
on the plastic surgery
if he's gonna cover it up

00:01:06.265 --> 00:01:08.201
with a mask?
[ Laughter ]

00:01:08.201 --> 00:01:09.835
-Yep, according to those
closest to him,

00:01:09.835 --> 00:01:13.172
Trump's never had any work done,
nor done any work.

00:01:13.172 --> 00:01:15.274
[ Laughter ]

00:01:15.274 --> 00:01:18.277
That's right, Trump made fun
of Biden's plastic surgery.

00:01:18.277 --> 00:01:20.713
Meanwhile, his handling
of the virus is about to appear

00:01:20.713 --> 00:01:22.615
on an episode of "Botched."

00:01:22.615 --> 00:01:24.116
[ Laughter ]

00:01:24.116 --> 00:01:27.153
By the way, did you see which
network was airing the rally?

00:01:27.153 --> 00:01:28.921
C-SPAN3.

00:01:28.921 --> 00:01:30.423
You know
your campaign's going well

00:01:30.423 --> 00:01:32.659
when even C-SPAN2 says,
"Nah, we're good."

00:01:32.659 --> 00:01:34.059
[ Laughter ]

00:01:34.059 --> 00:01:36.496
Meanwhile, in an interview
that aired last night on WGN,

00:01:36.496 --> 00:01:38.397
Trump was asked
what single quality

00:01:38.397 --> 00:01:41.101
he brings to the White House,
and here was his response.

00:01:46.339 --> 00:01:48.507
-Well, I think I bring an aura

00:01:48.507 --> 00:01:50.709
that people know
I know what I'm doing.

00:01:50.709 --> 00:01:52.545
I know what is happening.

00:01:52.545 --> 00:01:56.515
I know where we should be going,
I negotiate properly.

00:01:56.515 --> 00:01:58.151
I understand the military.

00:01:58.151 --> 00:02:00.419
I understand things
as a businessman

00:02:00.419 --> 00:02:01.587
that other people don't.

00:02:01.587 --> 00:02:04.557
Just as a person,
I understand things.

00:02:04.557 --> 00:02:08.695
-Yeah. Once again, the question
was, what single quality.

00:02:08.695 --> 00:02:11.030
[ Laughter ]

00:02:11.030 --> 00:02:13.132
Also, just because
you're glowing orange

00:02:13.132 --> 00:02:14.901
doesn't mean you have an aura.

00:02:14.901 --> 00:02:16.603
[ Laughter ]

00:02:16.603 --> 00:02:20.106
"I have an aura-ge, orange."

00:02:20.106 --> 00:02:22.075
That's right, Trump says
he knows what he's doing,

00:02:22.075 --> 00:02:24.711
what is happening,
and where he should be going.

00:02:24.711 --> 00:02:27.747
So, good news -- once again,
he passed concussion protocol.

00:02:27.747 --> 00:02:28.914
[ Laughter ]

00:02:28.914 --> 00:02:30.383
Seriously,
those are things you say

00:02:30.383 --> 00:02:32.985
after a trainer
gives you smelling salts.

00:02:32.985 --> 00:02:34.520
Well, guys,
we're just six days away

00:02:34.520 --> 00:02:36.022
from the first
presidential debate,

00:02:36.022 --> 00:02:38.257
and the topics Trump and Biden
will be discussing

00:02:38.257 --> 00:02:40.426
have been announced.
Check it out.

00:02:40.426 --> 00:02:42.161
-The moderator,
Fox News' Chris Wallace,

00:02:42.161 --> 00:02:44.730
has selected the six topics
that will be discussed.

00:02:44.730 --> 00:02:47.599
The topics include the
President's and Biden's records,

00:02:47.599 --> 00:02:51.604
the Supreme Court, coronavirus,
economic policy, racism,

00:02:51.604 --> 00:02:53.772
and the integrity
of the election.

00:02:53.772 --> 00:02:55.975
-That wasn't a good sign
when Trump's response was,

00:02:55.975 --> 00:02:59.112
"Pass, pass, pass,
pass, pass, and pass."

00:02:59.112 --> 00:03:00.346
[ Laughter ]

00:03:00.346 --> 00:03:01.747
Yeah, when Trump heard,
he was like,

00:03:01.747 --> 00:03:04.450
"I've got five more topics
that I'd love to talk about --

00:03:04.450 --> 00:03:08.388
man, woman, person, camera,
and TV."

00:03:08.388 --> 00:03:10.890
[ Laughter ]

00:03:10.890 --> 00:03:13.092
Right now,
it's just those topics

00:03:13.092 --> 00:03:14.927
and then the other
50 insane things that'll happen

00:03:14.927 --> 00:03:16.562
between now and Tuesday.

00:03:16.562 --> 00:03:17.963
Some more debate news,

00:03:17.963 --> 00:03:20.533
although this one is about
the vice presidential debate.

00:03:20.533 --> 00:03:23.036
It turns out Pete Buttigieg
has been standing in

00:03:23.036 --> 00:03:26.472
as Mike Pence for
Kamala Harris's debate practice.

00:03:26.472 --> 00:03:28.707
And to really get into the role
of Mike Pence,

00:03:28.707 --> 00:03:31.310
Buttigieg also wears three pairs
of Hanes long underwear

00:03:31.310 --> 00:03:32.745
safety pinned together.

00:03:32.745 --> 00:03:34.013
[ Laughter ]

00:03:34.013 --> 00:03:35.148
Speaking of Mike Pence,

00:03:35.148 --> 00:03:36.849
yesterday, his plane,
Air Force Two,

00:03:36.849 --> 00:03:38.618
was forced to return
to New Hampshire

00:03:38.618 --> 00:03:40.920
after it struck a bird.

00:03:40.920 --> 00:03:43.189
Actually, when Pence remembered
his debate against Kamala

00:03:43.189 --> 00:03:44.457
is only two weeks away,

00:03:44.457 --> 00:03:46.592
he started throwing more birds
into the engine.

00:03:46.592 --> 00:03:50.529
He's like, "Stop! Stop.
Help, stop, please."

00:03:50.529 --> 00:03:52.732
It's no surprise that birds
are attracted to Mike Pence.

00:03:52.732 --> 00:03:55.301
He's basically the human version
of white bread.

00:03:55.301 --> 00:03:57.737
[ Laughter ]

00:03:57.737 --> 00:04:00.673
Changing gears here,
this week, the CDC

00:04:00.673 --> 00:04:03.542
issued its first guidelines
for celebrating Halloween.

00:04:03.542 --> 00:04:05.611
Listen to this.
-The CDC released

00:04:05.611 --> 00:04:07.079
its recommendations
for Halloween,

00:04:07.079 --> 00:04:08.747
and the biggest one is to avoid

00:04:08.747 --> 00:04:10.750
traditional trick-or-treating
this year.

00:04:10.750 --> 00:04:13.352
The CDC also pointed out
that costume masks

00:04:13.352 --> 00:04:17.423
do not have the same protective
power as normal masks.

00:04:17.423 --> 00:04:19.425
-Remember the good old days
when all you had to worry about

00:04:19.425 --> 00:04:21.127
was a giant shiv
in your Snickers bar?

00:04:21.127 --> 00:04:26.466
[ Laughter ]

00:04:26.466 --> 00:04:28.768
The CDC is discouraging
trick-or-treating,

00:04:28.768 --> 00:04:31.337
but to be fair, maybe children
shouldn't have been going around

00:04:31.337 --> 00:04:33.873
collecting candy
from strangers anyway.

00:04:33.873 --> 00:04:35.308
That's right,
no trick-or-treating.

00:04:35.308 --> 00:04:36.742
It's too bad.
I'm really gonna miss

00:04:36.742 --> 00:04:38.644
the disappointed look
on my kids' face

00:04:38.644 --> 00:04:41.047
when they get an Almond Joy.

00:04:41.047 --> 00:04:43.616
[ Laughter ]

00:04:43.616 --> 00:04:47.587
I was fighting that joke.
I like Almond Joy. Yeah.

00:04:47.587 --> 00:04:48.955
-Yeah, no trick-or-treating.

00:04:48.955 --> 00:04:51.257
Kids will miss getting candy,
while parents will miss

00:04:51.257 --> 00:04:53.793
giving that quick judgy glimpse
into their neighbor's house.

00:04:53.793 --> 00:04:56.329
[ Laughter ]

00:04:56.329 --> 00:04:59.799
"Carpet in the kitchen?"
[ Laughter ]

00:04:59.799 --> 00:05:01.433
"Very '70s."

00:05:01.433 --> 00:05:04.503
Yep, the CDC is also
discouraging costume parties,

00:05:04.503 --> 00:05:06.338
mainly so no one
has to look at the idiot

00:05:06.338 --> 00:05:08.474
who dresses up
as the coronavirus.

00:05:08.474 --> 00:05:11.210
"Really funny, Carl."
[ Laughter ]

00:05:11.210 --> 00:05:12.545
Yeah, Halloween
will be different.

00:05:12.545 --> 00:05:14.379
If you see a house
covered in cobwebs,

00:05:14.379 --> 00:05:15.681
those aren't decorations.

00:05:15.681 --> 00:05:17.917
Those are people who haven't
gone outside since March.

00:05:17.917 --> 00:05:19.552
[ Laughter ]

00:05:19.552 --> 00:05:20.886
And finally, some sports news.

00:05:20.886 --> 00:05:22.055
A lot of people
are talking about

00:05:22.055 --> 00:05:23.756
Bill Belichick's sweatshirt

00:05:23.756 --> 00:05:25.524
from his press conference
this morning.

00:05:25.524 --> 00:05:29.395
Take a look at this.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:29.395 --> 00:05:30.630
Gosh, he looks like the Hulk

00:05:30.630 --> 00:05:32.231
after turning back
into Bruce Banner.

00:05:32.231 --> 00:05:34.733
[ Laughter ]

00:05:34.733 --> 00:05:37.036
Even crazier,
that's his wedding tuxedo.

00:05:37.036 --> 00:05:38.771
[ Laughter ]

00:05:38.771 --> 00:05:42.808
I think that shirt
was also established in 1960.

00:05:42.808 --> 00:05:44.010
I don't get it.

00:05:44.010 --> 00:05:45.845
Was he putting out cigarettes
on his shoulder?

00:05:45.845 --> 00:05:47.413
[ Laughter ]

00:05:47.413 --> 00:05:49.949
He looks like the centerfold
in "Divorced Dad Monthly."

00:05:49.949 --> 00:05:51.550
[ Laughter ]

00:05:51.550 --> 00:05:53.486
Remember that photo,
'cause it's what Chris Wallace

00:05:53.486 --> 00:05:55.588
is gonna look like
after Tuesday's debate.

00:05:55.588 --> 00:05:56.756
[ Laughter ]

